## Testing Database-Driven Applications

## The Core Strategy: Separate Concerns

```
Business Logic Layer  ←  tested with unit tests (mock DB)
Repository Layer      ←  tested with integration tests (real DB)
Database              ←  never hit in unit tests
```

## Step 1: Use the Repository Pattern

```typescript
// Define an interface — your business logic depends on the interface, not the DB
interface UserRepository {
  findById(id: string): Promise<User | null>;
  save(user: User): Promise<User>;
  delete(id: string): Promise<void>;
}

// Real implementation (used in production)
class SupabaseUserRepository implements UserRepository {
  async findById(id: string) {
    const { data } = await supabase.from('users').select().eq('id', id).single();
    return data;
  }
  // ...
}
```

## Step 2: Unit Test with a Mock Repository

```typescript
// Your business logic (easily testable)
class UserService {
  constructor(private repo: UserRepository) {}

  async deactivateUser(id: string): Promise<void> {
    const user = await this.repo.findById(id);
    if (!user) throw new Error('User not found');
    await this.repo.save({ ...user, active: false });
  }
}

// Unit test — no database
test('deactivateUser throws when user not found', async () => {
  const mockRepo: UserRepository = {
    findById: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue(null),
    save: jest.fn(),
    delete: jest.fn(),
  };
  const service = new UserService(mockRepo);

  await expect(service.deactivateUser('missing-id')).rejects.toThrow('User not found');
  expect(mockRepo.save).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
});
```

## Step 3: Integration Test with a Real Test Database

```typescript
// Uses a real Supabase test project / local Supabase
beforeEach(async () => {
  await testDb.from('users').delete().neq('id', ''); // clean slate
  await testDb.from('users').insert(testFixtures.users);
});

test('findById returns the correct user', async () => {
  const repo = new SupabaseUserRepository(testDb);
  const user = await repo.findById('fixture-user-1');
  expect(user?.name).toBe('Aaron');
});
```

## CI Setup

```yaml
# GitHub Actions example
services:
  postgres:
    image: postgres:15
    env:
      POSTGRES_DB: test_db
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: test
```

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

```
❌ Unit tests that hit a real database (slow, flaky, ordering issues)
❌ Sharing a database between tests (test pollution)
❌ Not cleaning up between tests (false positives/negatives)
❌ Mocking the ORM instead of the repository (too low-level)
```

## Summary

| Test Type | Database | What It Tests |
|---|---|---|
| Unit | Mocked repo | Business logic |
| Integration | Real test DB | Repository queries |
| E2E | Real test DB | Full user flow |

